From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: temporarily omit thread-pool-slow

The slow thread-pool test intermittently hangs in Azure Linux builds.
Enable the rest of the suite while the proposed idle-thread shutdown fix
awaits upstream acceptance. Remove this exclusion when the fix is adopted.

https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib/-/merge_requests/5484
https://dev.azure.com/mariner-org/mariner/_workitems/edit/24867

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [temporary downstream test exclusion]
---
 glib/tests/meson.build | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/glib/tests/meson.build b/glib/tests/meson.build
--- a/glib/tests/meson.build
+++ b/glib/tests/meson.build
@@ -169,7 +169,6 @@
   'thread' : {},
   'thread-deprecated' : {},
   'thread-pool' : {},
-  'thread-pool-slow' : {'suite' : ['slow']},
   'timeout' : {},
   'timer' : {},
   'tree' : {},
